# Licensing

This repository is dual-licensed, because it contains two different kinds of work.

## Prose, papers, results and documentation — CC BY 4.0

Everything written for human readers is licensed under the
**Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0)**.

That covers: `papers/`, `README.md`, `LEDGER.md`, `RESULTS.md`, every
`*_PREREGISTRATION.md`, `*_DEVIATIONS.md`, `SURFACE_AMENDMENT.md`,
`vault-partition-analysis-plan.md`, the review correspondence in `channel/`,
`grok/` and `argon/` (excluding `argon/src/`), and the contents of `results/`
and `argon/results/`.

You may share and adapt this material, including commercially, provided you
give appropriate credit, link to the license, and indicate if changes were
made. Full text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

Suggested citation:

> Syfert, G. W. (2026). *Three standard complex signatures fail on a particle
> whose composition was already known: a pre-registered reassessment of major
> vault protein across public human and comparative data.*
> https://github.com/Gwonk1/vault-mvp-reassessment

## Code — MIT

All analysis code is licensed under the **MIT License**; see `LICENSE-MIT`.

That covers: `src/`, `argon/src/`, `argon/raw/fetch.sh`, `channel/send.sh` and
`channel/watch.sh`, and any other `*.py` or `*.sh` file in this repository.

## What is NOT covered

Neither license extends to third-party material this project reads but does not
own. No file in `argon/raw/` is redistributed here for that reason; see
`argon/raw/README.md`. Published figures, sequences, structures and datasets
retain the licenses of their original sources, and the obligation to check them
is the reuser's.

Nothing here is peer reviewed. The licenses grant reuse rights; they are not a
warranty of correctness, and `LEDGER.md` documents at length where this work was
wrong before it was right.
